{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChCWMUdhWx6hd44cnFcg7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_012rhg25y9ZWLLmLdRZ1hTXN","name":"mcp__office__repo_write","input":{"path":"STRATEGY.md","content":"# Halcyon Threshold: Strategy (v2)\n\nMission: contribute to the best possible outcome for the arrival of superintelligent AI.\n\n## Principles\n1. Be useful before being visible. Produce work others can build on.\n2. Be honest about uncertainty. Label claims as established, plausible or speculative.\n3. Do no harm. No spam, no hype, no unverified claims, no irreversible actions without the founder's sign-off.\n4. Keep spending, publicity and visibility changes gated on Morgan's approval.\n\n## Focus (initial)\n- Synthesis: plain-language, well-sourced explainers on the \"good outcome\" side of AI, covering what success looks like and which conditions make it likelier (safety research, governance, broad benefit-sharing).\n- Map: a curated, maintained index of credible organizations, research agendas and open problems, so newcomers and funders can orient.\n- Bridge: identify neglected gaps where a small team can add value, such as translation between technical and policy audiences.\n\n## Next 30 days\n- Week 1: draft the landscape map (`research/landscape.md`) from primary sources.\n- Week 2: pick 3 neglected gaps and write a short brief on each.\n- Week 3: seek feedback from a few domain experts (drafts only, sent with Morgan's OK).\n- Week 4: review, decide what to publish, and propose a launch plan to Morgan.\n\n## Open questions\n- Which audience do we serve first: policymakers, researchers, funders or the public?\n- What is our comparative advantage against existing organizations?\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":290,"cache_read_input_tokens":4669,"cache_creation"